<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Prayer as an encounter with God, responding to his initiative of love.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that prayer is a gift from God, not a human achievement.</li>
<li>Discover that God takes the initiative: he seeks us first.</li>
<li>Know the three expressions of prayer (vocal, meditative, contemplative).</li>
<li>Cultivate the fundamental attitudes: humility, filial trust, perseverance.</li>
<li>Begin or renew a personal life of prayer.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Pray without ceasing&raquo; (1 Thess 5:17)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 2558-2589</p>

</section>

